1
00:00:00,160 --> 00:00:03,440
- Why are we even dating if
you’re going to keep ignoring me?

2
00:00:03,680 --> 00:00:06,680
- I’ve never seen anyone
drive you this crazy before.

3
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:08,039
- Should I stop doing what I want

4
00:00:08,039 --> 00:00:10,640
- and force myself to do silly things
just to please someone else?

5
00:00:11,680 --> 00:00:13,480
- Can you stop setting conditions

6
00:00:13,920 --> 00:00:18,400
- and just let things
happen based on how you feel?

7
00:00:18,720 --> 00:00:21,320
- I’ll admit that… I really like Moth.

8
00:00:22,160 --> 00:00:23,960
- I never felt like you weren’t important.

9
00:00:24,280 --> 00:00:25,240
- I’m really sorry.

10
00:00:26,440 --> 00:00:27,720
- Who are you, really?

11
00:00:27,800 --> 00:00:29,280
- I’m a maniac, I guess.

12
00:02:00,640 --> 00:02:01,640
Wait.

13
00:02:08,639 --> 00:02:10,120
Can I use the bathroom first?

14
00:04:10,480 --> 00:04:14,040
♪ I don’t know if you follow your heart too ♪

15
00:04:14,040 --> 00:04:17,680
♪ Or if you love me the way I love you ♪

16
00:04:17,680 --> 00:04:22,240
♪ Please give me a clue ♪

17
00:04:23,080 --> 00:04:27,920
♪ If I give my whole heart to loving only you ♪

18
00:04:27,920 --> 00:04:30,720
♪ Let it lead me all the way through ♪

19
00:04:30,760 --> 00:04:33,600
♪ Please make me feel secure ♪

20
00:04:33,600 --> 00:04:37,920
♪ Promise me your love will always endure ♪

21
00:04:37,920 --> 00:04:42,600
♪ I’ll use my heart to prove it’s true ♪

22
00:04:42,600 --> 00:04:46,480
♪ Even if I don’t know
Where this road leads to ♪

23
00:04:47,159 --> 00:04:55,200
♪ I believe my heart’s answer
Will always be you ♪

24
00:04:55,840 --> 00:04:57,880
(What can make people
fall in love with each other?)

25
00:04:59,120 --> 00:04:59,760
(Looks?)

26
00:05:02,360 --> 00:05:03,000
(Taste?)

27
00:05:05,800 --> 00:05:06,360
(Scent?)

28
00:05:10,000 --> 00:05:10,680
(Voice?)

29
00:05:11,360 --> 00:05:14,560
(Bagel: Actually, if your dog comes over
and leans against your leg…)

30
00:05:14,560 --> 00:05:16,160
[DOG LOVERS, EVER LOVED SOMEONE
SO MUCH YOU TURNED INTO A DOG?]
(Bagel: ...don’t go anywhere just yet.)

31
00:05:16,160 --> 00:05:19,000
[DOG LOVERS, EVER LOVED SOMEONE
SO MUCH YOU TURNED INTO A DOG?]
(Bagel: Your pup is telling you
this is a safe place.)

32
00:05:20,240 --> 00:05:20,800
(Right.)

33
00:05:20,800 --> 00:05:21,520
TWO MONTHS AGO

34
00:05:21,520 --> 00:05:23,760
(Who would’ve thought I’d fall in love
with someone because of his voice?)

35
00:05:24,240 --> 00:05:25,160
(It’s so damn crazy.)

36
00:05:25,360 --> 00:05:29,240
[BAGEL SMOKED SALMON’S SPEAKING.]
(Bagel: If their tails are stiff and wagging
rapidly, that means they’re being cautious.)

37
00:05:30,080 --> 00:05:33,080
(Bagel: So if you want to know
whether your dog is happy…)

38
00:05:33,080 --> 00:05:35,880
(Bagel: ...don’t just look at their tail.
Look at their eyes, too.)

39
00:05:57,240 --> 00:05:59,040
Why do dogs lick their paws?

40
00:05:59,040 --> 00:06:00,880
Anyone with a dog should know this.

41
00:06:01,120 --> 00:06:04,160
Dogs lick their paws because
something may be wrong with their health.

42
00:06:05,160 --> 00:06:07,240
Behaviors that show
dogs are attached to their owners

43
00:06:07,240 --> 00:06:08,680
What are eight things dogs shouldn’t eat?

44
00:06:08,680 --> 00:06:11,320
Today, I’m going to teach you
how to brush your dog’s teeth.

45
00:06:11,560 --> 00:06:13,600
First, pick up the toothbrush.

46
00:06:13,920 --> 00:06:19,600
If you can’t do it yourself,
Buddy Heal’s here to help every pup.

47
00:06:20,000 --> 00:06:22,680
One, your dog walks
or runs around in circles.

48
00:06:22,760 --> 00:06:23,680
That’s a sign…

49
00:06:23,680 --> 00:06:28,360
(Bagel: I don’t know if I’ve turned into a dog,
but I’ve got a story of my own, too.)

50
00:06:31,760 --> 00:06:32,360
Match!

51
00:06:33,120 --> 00:06:34,360
(Bagel: Well... )

52
00:06:35,480 --> 00:06:37,480
(Bagel: I have a secret crush
on a close friend.)

53
00:06:39,560 --> 00:06:40,880
(Bagel: He’s an artist.)

54
00:06:41,520 --> 00:06:42,960
(Bagel: He hates chaos.)

55
00:06:43,440 --> 00:06:44,520
(Bagel: And he’s pretty dense.)

56
00:06:44,840 --> 00:06:46,440
[DOG LOVERS, EVER LOVED SOMEONE
SO MUCH YOU TURNED INTO A DOG?]

57
00:06:46,440 --> 00:06:48,360
(Bagel: I try to show him that I like him.)
[DOG LOVERS, EVER LOVED SOMEONE
SO MUCH YOU TURNED INTO A DOG?]

58
00:06:49,320 --> 00:06:51,600
(Bagel: He’s the only person I tag on Instagram.)

59
00:07:08,560 --> 00:07:10,480
(What’s even crazier is that…)

60
00:07:12,000 --> 00:07:15,840
(I fell in love
and got my heart broken instantly.)

61
00:07:22,320 --> 00:07:24,080
(And you know what the craziest thing is?)

62
00:07:24,200 --> 00:07:25,000
What?

63
00:07:25,480 --> 00:07:28,160
(You calling me first thing in the morning
with your nonsense, dickhead.)

64
00:07:29,360 --> 00:07:30,200
(What’s wrong with you?)

65
00:07:30,200 --> 00:07:31,720
(All you do is gush about him all day.)

66
00:07:33,000 --> 00:07:34,080
I’ve had enough.

67
00:07:34,320 --> 00:07:35,320
(I need to stop.)

68
00:07:35,560 --> 00:07:39,520
It’s time I accepted that he and I…

69
00:07:40,920 --> 00:07:42,440
can only go so far.

70
00:07:43,000 --> 00:07:44,280
(You can’t say that.)

71
00:07:44,520 --> 00:07:45,960
You haven’t gotten anywhere with him yet.

72
00:07:46,120 --> 00:07:47,680
You can stop hitting on Moth.

73
00:07:47,880 --> 00:07:49,159
I’m over him, dude.

74
00:07:50,720 --> 00:07:51,600
Fine.

75
00:07:55,440 --> 00:07:56,640
Where are you, anyway?

76
00:07:57,440 --> 00:07:58,920
What’s with that horny voice?

77
00:07:58,920 --> 00:07:59,840
Horny, my ass.

78
00:08:00,480 --> 00:08:01,160
I’m just whispering.

79
00:08:01,920 --> 00:08:02,840
Yeah, that.

80
00:08:03,120 --> 00:08:04,960
Why are you whispering?

81
00:08:06,760 --> 00:08:07,720
Moth’s sleeping.

82
00:08:13,640 --> 00:08:14,520
I’m hanging up now.

83
00:08:30,760 --> 00:08:32,120
[TEN: WHAT ARE YOU DOING?]
[PUN: I’M WORKING.]

84
00:08:32,120 --> 00:08:33,440
[TEN: HAVE YOU EATEN?]
[PUN: I HAVE. YOU?]

85
00:08:33,440 --> 00:08:34,640
[TEN: I ALREADY HAVE TOO.]
[PUN: SENT A STICKER.]

86
00:08:37,480 --> 00:08:38,600
[TEN: GOING FOR A RUN TODAY?]
[PUN: MY ANKLE HURTS.]

87
00:08:38,600 --> 00:08:39,440
[TEN: YOU’VE BEEN BUSY LATELY?]

88
00:08:39,440 --> 00:08:40,360
[TEN: WILL YOU BE AT THE CLINIC TODAY?]

89
00:08:40,360 --> 00:08:41,159
[TEN: YOU’VE BEEN BUSY?]

90
00:08:41,159 --> 00:08:41,880
[PUN: SORRY, TEN.
I’VE BEEN SWAMPED.]

91
00:08:47,600 --> 00:08:48,720
[TEN: THAT’S OKAY.]

92
00:08:48,720 --> 00:08:49,960
[TEN: GOOD MORNING.]

93
00:09:02,080 --> 00:09:04,680
(Hong: Why are you up so early, Mr. Bagel?)
[IT’S FINE IF THEY DON’T LOVE US—
OUR DOGS DO!]

94
00:09:04,680 --> 00:09:08,000
(Bagel: I usually get up early.
I’m having breakfast, too.)

95
00:09:08,240 --> 00:09:09,280
(Bagel: I was feeling a little lonely…)

96
00:09:09,280 --> 00:09:10,640
(Bagel: …so I came here
to chat with you guys.)
[PUN: SORRY, TEN.
I’VE BEEN SWAMPED.]

97
00:09:10,640 --> 00:09:13,240
(Hong: Great.
We missed your voice. Mr. Bagel.)

98
00:09:13,240 --> 00:09:15,160
(Hong: I actually have a question for you, Mr. Bagel.)

99
00:09:15,160 --> 00:09:17,080
(Hong: My dog looks really drowsy.)

100
00:09:17,360 --> 00:09:19,160
(Hong: I don’t know if it’s because
his stomach is bloated)

101
00:09:19,360 --> 00:09:21,480
(Hong: …or because I haven’t had
enough time to take him out for a run.)

102
00:09:21,520 --> 00:09:24,760
(Sean: Of course. I bet you spend all your time courting that guy.)

103
00:09:24,800 --> 00:09:26,080
(Bagel: What guy, Mr. Sean?)

104
00:09:26,080 --> 00:09:28,680
(Bagel: Mr. Hong, are you in love?)

105
00:09:28,800 --> 00:09:30,840
(Bagel: You can share
your story with us if you want.)

106
00:11:32,080 --> 00:11:32,720
Shit.

107
00:11:34,680 --> 00:11:36,120
Do you have to be so harsh?

108
00:11:38,480 --> 00:11:40,880
I thought you left.

109
00:11:48,680 --> 00:11:49,720
How could I leave?

110
00:11:54,160 --> 00:11:55,320
The job isn’t finished yet.

111
00:12:05,640 --> 00:12:07,240
I went downstairs to buy something.

112
00:12:09,200 --> 00:12:11,080
What you have isn’t my size.

113
00:12:36,640 --> 00:12:37,640
You don’t want to?

114
00:12:46,000 --> 00:12:46,680
Okay.

115
00:12:47,960 --> 00:12:48,840
I understand.

116
00:12:50,200 --> 00:12:51,040
It’s fine.

117
00:13:06,840 --> 00:13:08,160
You said the job isn’t finished?

118
00:13:10,200 --> 00:13:10,880
Then finish it.

119
00:13:29,040 --> 00:13:30,240
Do you like it soft...

120
00:13:30,800 --> 00:13:32,040
or rough?

121
00:13:40,120 --> 00:13:41,600
Surprise me.

122
00:13:56,400 --> 00:13:57,160
Answer it.

123
00:14:05,880 --> 00:14:06,520
Hello?

124
00:14:09,000 --> 00:14:10,080
Today at 10?

125
00:14:11,880 --> 00:14:12,960
Let me call you back.

126
00:14:19,240 --> 00:14:19,800
Work?

127
00:14:21,520 --> 00:14:22,280
Mhm.

128
00:14:23,880 --> 00:14:27,800
My client wants to
move our meeting from 1 to 10.

129
00:14:29,000 --> 00:14:30,240
Otherwise, we’ll have to push it to next week.

130
00:14:32,160 --> 00:14:34,760
So you have to leave now?

131
00:14:38,040 --> 00:14:38,720
Mm.

132
00:14:43,800 --> 00:14:46,960
Why don’t you push it to next week then?

133
00:14:59,080 --> 00:14:59,920
Just go to work.

134
00:15:17,640 --> 00:15:18,400
Why are you following me?

135
00:15:19,240 --> 00:15:20,000
Aren’t you going home?

136
00:15:21,400 --> 00:15:22,400
I am going home.

137
00:15:23,440 --> 00:15:23,760
What?

138
00:15:24,840 --> 00:15:25,720
Do you think I’m taking you to work?

139
00:15:27,760 --> 00:15:28,360
No.

140
00:15:38,840 --> 00:15:39,520
Whoa.

141
00:15:40,600 --> 00:15:41,960
Rough hand you’ve got.

142
00:15:43,880 --> 00:15:45,000
Did you have a rough childhood?

143
00:15:45,440 --> 00:15:46,640
I had a perfectly normal childhood.

144
00:15:47,360 --> 00:15:48,760
But I slap people in the face a lot.

145
00:15:48,760 --> 00:15:49,760
That’s why my hands are rough.

146
00:15:52,160 --> 00:15:52,920
I’m kidding.

147
00:15:58,200 --> 00:16:00,080
Did I hurt your self-esteem?

148
00:16:02,520 --> 00:16:04,480
Do I look like someone
so easy to lose self-esteem?

149
00:16:08,960 --> 00:16:10,080
Want me to read your palm?

150
00:16:11,960 --> 00:16:12,720
Can you?

151
00:16:14,480 --> 00:16:15,560
What kind of person are you?

152
00:16:15,880 --> 00:16:17,360
You always answer a question
with another question.

153
00:16:17,720 --> 00:16:18,080
Hey.

154
00:16:19,040 --> 00:16:20,960
I was just making sure
you could actually read palms

155
00:16:21,320 --> 00:16:22,680
and weren’t just making
an excuse to hold my hand.

156
00:16:24,120 --> 00:16:26,400
I don’t need an excuse to hold your hand.

157
00:16:27,480 --> 00:16:30,120
You’ve already let me
do a lot more than that.

158
00:16:37,560 --> 00:16:41,920
Your head line and heart line meet.

159
00:16:42,320 --> 00:16:43,920
That means you’re stubborn.

160
00:16:45,280 --> 00:16:46,280
Uncompromising.

161
00:16:48,120 --> 00:16:49,040
Headstrong.

162
00:16:49,720 --> 00:16:50,480
But cute.

163
00:16:53,120 --> 00:16:53,840
Jeez.

164
00:16:54,560 --> 00:16:55,480
Load of nonsense.

165
00:16:56,840 --> 00:16:59,080
Gosh, you never believe anything I say.

166
00:17:01,280 --> 00:17:03,160
When will you be done with work?

167
00:17:03,600 --> 00:17:04,920
Around 1 PM, I guess.

168
00:17:05,480 --> 00:17:06,040
Want me to wait for you?

169
00:17:07,680 --> 00:17:08,440
Why would you wait?

170
00:17:08,839 --> 00:17:11,079
So we can finish it.

171
00:17:15,240 --> 00:17:16,839
I have work in the afternoon.

172
00:17:17,720 --> 00:17:18,720
And when will you be done?

173
00:17:19,800 --> 00:17:20,480
I don’t know.

174
00:17:22,839 --> 00:17:23,920
How about tonight?

175
00:17:25,079 --> 00:17:26,000
I promise I won’t fall asleep.

176
00:17:36,000 --> 00:17:37,080
Get yourself ready.

177
00:17:38,320 --> 00:17:39,760
But don’t take as long as you did last night.

178
00:17:56,880 --> 00:17:57,960
You said you were going home.

179
00:17:58,880 --> 00:17:59,640
Why are you here?

180
00:17:59,920 --> 00:18:02,600
You still haven’t told me
when we’ll meet again.

181
00:18:03,720 --> 00:18:05,200
I told you tonight isn’t a good time.

182
00:18:06,800 --> 00:18:07,680
How about tomorrow?

183
00:18:09,000 --> 00:18:10,680
Can I check my schedule first?

184
00:18:12,760 --> 00:18:13,800
And what’s this?

185
00:18:14,560 --> 00:18:16,120
Why are you so eager for an answer?

186
00:18:17,320 --> 00:18:18,520
Because we’ve put this off for quite a while.

187
00:18:18,720 --> 00:18:20,040
What if you change your mind?

188
00:18:20,040 --> 00:18:20,840
What will I do?

189
00:18:21,680 --> 00:18:21,960
Huh?

190
00:18:23,200 --> 00:18:24,480
I want to finish it with you.

191
00:18:26,400 --> 00:18:27,280
And after that?

192
00:18:29,000 --> 00:18:29,720
After that?

193
00:18:30,640 --> 00:18:31,400
What about after that?

194
00:18:35,760 --> 00:18:36,440
Let’s say Saturday.

195
00:18:36,800 --> 00:18:38,040
Oh, come on. Saturday?

196
00:18:39,440 --> 00:18:40,200
It’s only Monday.

197
00:18:41,680 --> 00:18:42,960
Think of it as being a kid again.

198
00:18:44,080 --> 00:18:47,520
Be a good kid for five days,
then come see me on Saturday.

199
00:18:54,120 --> 00:18:54,760
What now?

200
00:18:55,960 --> 00:18:57,280
We still have 15 minutes left.

201
00:18:58,000 --> 00:19:01,040
How about we find somewhere around here
and get it over with?

202
00:19:13,680 --> 00:19:15,200
[CAN WE DO IT ON WEDNESDAY?]

203
00:19:15,200 --> 00:19:16,360
[SATURDAY IS TOO FAR AWAY.]

204
00:19:16,360 --> 00:19:18,800
So these are the characters
that we talked about.

205
00:19:18,960 --> 00:19:19,360
Moth.

206
00:19:19,960 --> 00:19:20,640
Moth.

207
00:19:22,960 --> 00:19:23,400
Yes?

208
00:19:24,240 --> 00:19:24,880
Pardon?

209
00:19:27,000 --> 00:19:28,720
Can you submit the first draft
by the beginning of next month?

210
00:19:29,120 --> 00:19:30,320
I only need the main characters.

211
00:19:30,640 --> 00:19:32,240
Ah, of course.

212
00:19:35,480 --> 00:19:37,320
[MISSING YOU LIKE CRAZY OVER HERE.]

213
00:19:50,760 --> 00:19:53,760
[WHAT ARE YOU DOING TONIGHT?]

214
00:19:55,800 --> 00:20:00,680
[I TOLD YOU. SATURDAY.]

215
00:20:00,800 --> 00:20:04,480
[BUT I CAN’T WAIT UNTIL SATURDAY.]

216
00:20:08,120 --> 00:20:09,000
(Are you free today?)

217
00:20:09,520 --> 00:20:10,440
What day is it today?

218
00:20:10,880 --> 00:20:11,840
Saturday.

219
00:20:12,000 --> 00:20:12,960
Don’t play dumb.

220
00:20:13,120 --> 00:20:14,320
Are you free, though?

221
00:20:14,320 --> 00:20:15,440
(It doesn’t matter if I’m free.)

222
00:20:15,440 --> 00:20:17,520
(We said Saturday. Stick to it.)

223
00:20:40,640 --> 00:20:42,400
[WHAT ARE YOU DOING?]

224
00:20:43,760 --> 00:20:45,600
[WANT TO MEET ME TONIGHT?]

225
00:20:48,040 --> 00:20:51,840
[I’M JUST ASKING WHAT YOU’RE DOING.]

226
00:20:51,840 --> 00:20:52,760
How about some photos?

227
00:20:54,080 --> 00:20:55,600
Scooch in a little closer.

228
00:21:08,280 --> 00:21:09,240
Don’t be so hard on yourself.

229
00:21:09,400 --> 00:21:10,840
It’s not the first time
you’ve hit a creative block.

230
00:21:11,400 --> 00:21:14,440
That’s true, but this time is different.

231
00:21:15,480 --> 00:21:18,080
I can’t think straight. I can’t focus.

232
00:21:19,040 --> 00:21:21,520
Maybe your focus is somewhere else?

233
00:21:24,440 --> 00:21:25,880
Why do you have to look so whiny?

234
00:21:26,200 --> 00:21:27,200
I was just asking.

235
00:21:33,920 --> 00:21:34,520
Okay.

236
00:21:36,320 --> 00:21:38,280
Try going out and having some fun.

237
00:21:39,120 --> 00:21:40,160
The idea will come to you eventually.

238
00:22:10,480 --> 00:22:11,600
The world must be ending.

239
00:22:11,880 --> 00:22:12,880
You’re actually calling me.

240
00:22:14,680 --> 00:22:15,440
Are you free tomorrow?

241
00:22:16,760 --> 00:22:18,680
(I am.)

242
00:22:19,080 --> 00:22:22,360
How about we meet tomorrow?

243
00:22:29,200 --> 00:22:29,920
Sure.

244
00:22:31,280 --> 00:22:31,840
See you then.

245
00:22:44,600 --> 00:22:46,840
I’m telling you, this is a hidden gem
you don’t want to miss.

246
00:22:46,840 --> 00:22:49,280
And where will Everydeanlive
take you next time?

247
00:22:49,280 --> 00:22:50,360
Stay tuned to find out.

248
00:22:53,080 --> 00:22:53,840
Okay.

249
00:23:02,880 --> 00:23:04,600
[DON’T FORGET ABOUT TONIGHT.]

250
00:23:07,040 --> 00:23:08,680
[SHOULD WE MEET AT THE CLUB FIRST?]

251
00:23:11,120 --> 00:23:13,320
[NO. JUST COME TO MY PLACE.]

252
00:23:14,560 --> 00:23:15,760
[WHAT TIME?]

253
00:23:18,840 --> 00:23:20,320
[EVENING.]

254
00:23:20,840 --> 00:23:22,800
[DON’T FORGET.
IT’S MY BIRTHDAY TODAY.]

255
00:23:23,000 --> 00:23:24,600
[INVITE TEN ALONG, TOO.]

256
00:23:28,440 --> 00:23:30,480
[OKAY.]

257
00:23:42,640 --> 00:23:44,000
Want to go to Max’s birthday party?

258
00:23:45,840 --> 00:23:46,640
Max who?

259
00:23:47,160 --> 00:23:51,120
The guy who went on that road trip
to Chiang Mai with us in second year.

260
00:23:51,360 --> 00:23:52,440
Who would remember him?

261
00:23:52,440 --> 00:23:53,760
He remembers you.

262
00:23:54,280 --> 00:23:56,120
He asked me to invite you too.

263
00:23:57,840 --> 00:23:58,960
But I don’t think I’ll go.

264
00:23:59,480 --> 00:24:02,280
What? If you’re not going, neither am I.

265
00:24:03,000 --> 00:24:05,640
But why aren’t you going?

266
00:24:06,280 --> 00:24:08,000
You never miss stuff like this.

267
00:24:09,880 --> 00:24:10,840
I have plans with Moth.

268
00:24:13,640 --> 00:24:14,640
So you’re going to finish the job?

269
00:24:17,200 --> 00:24:18,760
And what happens after tonight?

270
00:24:18,880 --> 00:24:22,400
Will you two go your separate ways,
or end up as friends like the others?

271
00:24:22,400 --> 00:24:24,280
Why are you so nosy
about my business? Huh?

272
00:24:27,040 --> 00:24:29,640
You’ve made me waste so many days.

273
00:24:30,720 --> 00:24:32,000
You said you’d go after Dr. Pun.

274
00:24:32,760 --> 00:24:33,160
You dipshit.

275
00:24:33,720 --> 00:24:35,200
You let him slip away.

276
00:24:38,960 --> 00:24:39,560
Yeah.

277
00:24:41,800 --> 00:24:42,680
You don’t have to rub it in my face.

278
00:26:16,360 --> 00:26:17,080
(Where are you?)

279
00:26:17,680 --> 00:26:19,480
Let me swing by
my friend’s birthday party first.

280
00:26:20,280 --> 00:26:21,320
But we have plans!

281
00:26:22,400 --> 00:26:23,640
(I’ll come over after this.)

282
00:26:24,680 --> 00:26:25,520
What time?

283
00:26:26,440 --> 00:26:28,640
Two in the morning, I guess.

284
00:26:28,760 --> 00:26:29,320
What?

285
00:26:29,680 --> 00:26:30,720
You expect me to wait that long?

286
00:26:31,520 --> 00:26:33,440
I asked you what time, but you didn’t answer.

287
00:26:34,000 --> 00:26:35,040
I said evening.

288
00:26:35,840 --> 00:26:37,360
Can’t your brain figure out
what “evening” means?

289
00:26:39,000 --> 00:26:39,920
Fine, let’s say midnight.

290
00:26:42,280 --> 00:26:43,240
What the hell is this?

291
00:26:43,880 --> 00:26:44,760
Then come out and join me.

292
00:26:45,120 --> 00:26:47,400
Hang out together and go home together.

293
00:26:47,640 --> 00:26:48,560
Which friend of yours
is having a birthday party?

294
00:26:49,440 --> 00:26:50,920
Ohm, Boom, or Hun?

295
00:26:50,960 --> 00:26:51,680
None of them.

296
00:26:52,320 --> 00:26:52,960
Someone else.

297
00:26:52,960 --> 00:26:54,920
What? Then I don’t know them.

298
00:26:54,920 --> 00:26:55,880
How am I supposed to show up?

299
00:26:55,880 --> 00:26:57,040
Of course you can come.

300
00:26:57,240 --> 00:26:58,520
Ohm and Boom are here, too.

301
00:26:59,560 --> 00:27:01,640
Take your pick. What do you want to do?

302
00:27:02,240 --> 00:27:03,440
Do you want to stay at your friend’s party?

303
00:27:03,600 --> 00:27:06,200
What the heck? Don’t be ridiculous.

304
00:27:07,080 --> 00:27:07,920
Come meet me here.

305
00:27:08,440 --> 00:27:08,920
No.

306
00:27:09,320 --> 00:27:10,240
Just stay with your friends.

307
00:27:10,720 --> 00:27:11,400
Bye.

308
00:27:37,440 --> 00:27:41,720
Happy birthday!

309
00:28:02,120 --> 00:28:03,480
(Hello, Mr. Monsieur.)

310
00:28:03,480 --> 00:28:04,920
(You’re online pretty late tonight.)

311
00:28:04,920 --> 00:28:07,280
(Will we finally get to hear
Mr. Monsieur’s voice tonight?)

312
00:28:07,280 --> 00:28:07,920
(No way.)

313
00:28:08,040 --> 00:28:11,280
(He only ever joins to listen.
He never says a word.)

314
00:28:11,880 --> 00:28:13,800
[IT’S FINE IF THEY DON’T LOVE US—
OUR DOGS DO!]
(There aren’t many members tonight.
Say something.)

315
00:28:13,800 --> 00:28:15,960
(You know, Mr. Bagel is heartbroken again.)

316
00:28:16,080 --> 00:28:17,400
(Help us cheer him up.)

317
00:28:18,120 --> 00:28:21,440
Mr. Monsieur has probably heard
this story a hundred times by now.

318
00:28:21,760 --> 00:28:23,040
He must be sick of it.

319
00:28:24,480 --> 00:28:26,880
(I’m heading to bed, though.
I have to get up early.)

320
00:28:27,360 --> 00:28:28,440
(I’m leaving too.)

321
00:28:28,880 --> 00:28:30,200
(Bye, Mr. Bagel.)

322
00:28:31,240 --> 00:28:33,160
(What? They’re all gone.)

323
00:28:34,560 --> 00:28:36,200
It’s just the two of us now.

324
00:28:39,000 --> 00:28:41,000
Let’s close the chat room, then.

325
00:28:42,760 --> 00:28:44,080
Wait, Mr. Bagel!

326
00:28:55,240 --> 00:28:55,800
Hey.

327
00:28:57,280 --> 00:29:00,080
Mr. Monsieur finally spoke.

328
00:29:04,040 --> 00:29:06,920
Mr. Bagel, are you getting sleepy?

329
00:29:08,760 --> 00:29:09,640
No.

330
00:29:10,560 --> 00:29:12,320
I’m actually still at work.

331
00:29:12,840 --> 00:29:16,600
You’re usually quiet,
so I thought you’d be bored.

332
00:29:17,360 --> 00:29:20,200
Why aren’t you home yet, Mr. Bagel?

333
00:29:20,360 --> 00:29:23,720
I was afraid I’d spiral
in my own head if I went home.

334
00:29:24,360 --> 00:29:25,920
So I joined the chat.

335
00:29:26,320 --> 00:29:27,520
Then I got a little carried away.

336
00:29:28,560 --> 00:29:31,200
Mr. Monsieur, aren’t you sleepy?

337
00:29:31,320 --> 00:29:31,920
No.

338
00:29:33,280 --> 00:29:35,560
I can’t sleep either.

339
00:29:35,760 --> 00:29:39,280
Good. Then you can keep me company.

340
00:29:39,760 --> 00:29:42,960
Are you overthinking things
with that friend of yours?

341
00:29:43,320 --> 00:29:44,720
Is that what’s keeping you up?

342
00:29:46,080 --> 00:29:49,040
Wow. You barely say a word,

343
00:29:49,360 --> 00:29:51,800
but you’ve been following
my story this whole time, huh?

344
00:30:04,760 --> 00:30:05,560
Bye-bye.

345
00:30:16,720 --> 00:30:19,360
What did he do today
to break your heart again?

346
00:30:20,560 --> 00:30:21,920
Nothing, really.

347
00:30:22,840 --> 00:30:27,760
He’s just alone with someone at his place.

348
00:30:31,360 --> 00:30:34,680
I’m sure I don’t have to tell you
what they’re doing.

349
00:30:40,200 --> 00:30:42,080
I’m such a big mess.

350
00:30:43,160 --> 00:30:48,600
I chose to be in this kind of relationship,
and now I’m upset about it.

351
00:30:51,400 --> 00:30:54,080
It might not be what you think.

352
00:30:54,760 --> 00:30:55,960
Maybe…

353
00:30:56,720 --> 00:31:00,360
that guy ditched your friend and went to
his friend’s birthday party instead.

354
00:31:04,080 --> 00:31:06,160
Oh! I’m just guessing. I have no idea.

355
00:31:06,640 --> 00:31:09,480
I don’t know you,
and I don’t know your friend.

356
00:31:10,320 --> 00:31:14,640
Ah, I thought someone in my real life
was spying on me.

357
00:31:17,040 --> 00:31:20,440
(Honestly, your voice sounds so familiar.)

358
00:31:23,200 --> 00:31:24,800
You sound like someone I know.

359
00:31:25,680 --> 00:31:29,920
Maybe you are...

360
00:31:29,920 --> 00:31:32,760
I’m… who?

361
00:31:39,560 --> 00:31:40,600
I’m just kidding.

362
00:31:41,720 --> 00:31:43,520
(I don’t think we know each other in real life.)

363
00:31:44,160 --> 00:31:49,040
If someone I know found out
how ridiculous I am in this chat,

364
00:31:49,920 --> 00:31:51,480
I wouldn’t know how to face them.

365
00:31:58,560 --> 00:31:59,720
It’s okay.

366
00:32:00,520 --> 00:32:04,440
Humans don’t have to be strong all the time.

367
00:32:12,120 --> 00:32:15,920
I don’t even know why I have to be strong.

368
00:32:19,080 --> 00:32:23,600
(But thank you so much, Mr. Monsieur,
for keeping me company.)

369
00:32:24,360 --> 00:32:27,760
And… it’s nice getting to know you.

370
00:32:29,080 --> 00:32:32,480
I’m glad I got to talk to you, too, Mr. Bagel.

371
00:33:09,680 --> 00:33:10,040
Hey.

372
00:33:10,760 --> 00:33:11,720
You said you weren’t coming.

373
00:33:12,800 --> 00:33:14,400
I was alone and had nothing to do.

374
00:33:14,640 --> 00:33:15,440
Who did you come with?

375
00:33:15,640 --> 00:33:16,440
You came alone?

376
00:33:18,200 --> 00:33:19,360
Why ask when you already know?

377
00:33:20,720 --> 00:33:21,840
You don’t have to be so snappy.

378
00:33:22,960 --> 00:33:23,840
Come join my friends.

379
00:33:24,320 --> 00:33:25,240
I told you, I don’t know them.

380
00:33:26,080 --> 00:33:27,520
Ohm and Boom are there, too.

381
00:33:30,920 --> 00:33:31,560
Come on.

382
00:33:32,160 --> 00:33:33,360
Stop f*cking bothering me.

383
00:33:33,920 --> 00:33:34,960
Go do whatever you want.

384
00:33:36,200 --> 00:33:37,040
I want to be alone.

385
00:33:39,920 --> 00:33:40,920
Can you talk nicely?

386
00:33:41,280 --> 00:33:42,040
I’m asking you.

387
00:33:44,440 --> 00:33:44,960
Fine.

388
00:33:46,640 --> 00:33:47,320
Piss off.

389
00:33:50,400 --> 00:33:52,320
Waiter, a glass of beer.

390
00:33:56,200 --> 00:33:56,680
Fine.

391
00:33:58,120 --> 00:33:58,760
Suit yourself.

392
00:34:17,840 --> 00:34:19,679
I told you to stay away
from my boy, you motherf*cker!

393
00:34:21,280 --> 00:34:22,480
- Just calm down, Max.
- Calm down, my ass!

394
00:34:22,480 --> 00:34:23,960
You wanna hook up with everyone? Huh?

395
00:34:24,000 --> 00:34:24,880
What the f*ck is wrong with you?

396
00:34:25,120 --> 00:34:25,600
You f*cker!

397
00:34:25,600 --> 00:34:25,960
Shit!

398
00:34:26,639 --> 00:34:27,520
Max, what the hell are you doing?

399
00:34:27,520 --> 00:34:28,239
Let go.

400
00:34:28,239 --> 00:34:28,600
Max!

401
00:34:30,159 --> 00:34:30,600
Easy!

402
00:34:30,600 --> 00:34:31,520
Let go of me.

403
00:34:33,520 --> 00:34:34,239
What are you looking at?

404
00:34:34,239 --> 00:34:35,400
Let go!

405
00:34:35,400 --> 00:34:37,040
Dean, just leave for now.

406
00:34:38,320 --> 00:34:39,199
Step outside!

407
00:34:39,679 --> 00:34:40,600
Take it easy!

408
00:35:13,000 --> 00:35:15,320
Does it taste good,
blood and booze together?

409
00:35:17,320 --> 00:35:21,200
Did you enjoy watching all that drama?

410
00:35:22,480 --> 00:35:23,800
Still got a nice mouth, I see.

411
00:35:27,000 --> 00:35:29,280
So, is this how it ends for a hot guy?

412
00:35:48,400 --> 00:35:49,560
Do you want to see a doctor?

413
00:35:50,720 --> 00:35:51,240
Mm.

414
00:35:51,720 --> 00:35:54,320
Let me think about
which doctor I should see.

415
00:35:54,840 --> 00:35:57,960
I do know a doctor nearby,
but he’s not very cute.

416
00:35:59,040 --> 00:36:00,280
I’ll just find someone inside.

417
00:36:02,000 --> 00:36:03,000
Flirt my way into getting him.

418
00:36:05,520 --> 00:36:07,720
Right. That’s just how assholes do things.

419
00:36:18,960 --> 00:36:19,800
Should we go back to your place?

420
00:36:21,920 --> 00:36:22,800
To finish it?

421
00:36:26,280 --> 00:36:26,960
No need.

422
00:36:27,160 --> 00:36:27,880
It’s already over.

423
00:36:41,320 --> 00:36:42,080
Where’s Dean?

424
00:36:43,800 --> 00:36:46,040
I couldn’t deal with him, so I left him outside.

425
00:36:48,400 --> 00:36:49,200
How’s it going in here?

426
00:36:51,040 --> 00:36:52,200
He’s calmed down.

427
00:36:53,440 --> 00:36:54,680
And his boy already left, too.

428
00:36:55,240 --> 00:36:55,560
What?

429
00:36:57,200 --> 00:36:57,720
Why?

430
00:36:58,360 --> 00:36:59,680
Max got the wrong idea.

431
00:37:00,040 --> 00:37:02,280
Dean never messed with
the guy he’s seeing.

432
00:38:18,720 --> 00:38:22,240
GY 0619
RATCHABURI

433
00:38:47,280 --> 00:38:48,480
Damn it!

434
00:39:10,840 --> 00:39:13,320
You’re lucky I didn’t call the cops.

435
00:39:14,760 --> 00:39:16,040
I didn’t want to wake you.

436
00:39:16,240 --> 00:39:18,600
Even after you just got into a fight?

437
00:39:19,240 --> 00:39:20,760
You’re getting worse every day.

438
00:39:21,320 --> 00:39:22,920
You never tell anyone anything.

439
00:39:22,920 --> 00:39:24,160
Not just Mom and Dad.

440
00:39:25,160 --> 00:39:26,160
Now you’re keeping secrets from me, too?

441
00:39:27,320 --> 00:39:30,520
You didn’t tell me
you were coming to Bangkok either.

442
00:39:31,240 --> 00:39:32,240
How could I tell you?

443
00:39:33,240 --> 00:39:34,720
Do you ever answer my calls?

444
00:39:35,960 --> 00:39:37,600
You don’t even read my texts.

445
00:39:42,640 --> 00:39:44,000
I came for my friend’s wedding.

446
00:39:44,280 --> 00:39:45,520
I’m going home tomorrow.

447
00:39:46,400 --> 00:39:48,440
Not staying around to bother you.
Don’t worry.

448
00:39:57,560 --> 00:40:01,120
I bet you’re not
going to tell me what happened.

449
00:40:03,880 --> 00:40:07,960
If Mom found out you got into a fight,

450
00:40:07,960 --> 00:40:10,560
she’d be so stressed
she wouldn’t be able to eat for days.

451
00:40:11,200 --> 00:40:12,480
And why would you tell her?

452
00:40:15,080 --> 00:40:17,360
Mom needs to stop
expecting things from me.

453
00:40:19,680 --> 00:40:23,120
Mom doesn’t expect anything from you.

454
00:40:25,960 --> 00:40:28,360
She just wants her old son back.

455
00:40:29,280 --> 00:40:29,920
That’s all.

456
00:41:05,200 --> 00:41:08,000
[WHEN DID YOU LEAVE?]

457
00:41:08,000 --> 00:41:10,840
[ARE YOU OKAY?]

458
00:41:18,640 --> 00:41:24,560
[I’M SORRY…]

459
00:41:34,040 --> 00:41:35,040
Dean isn’t replying?

460
00:41:37,320 --> 00:41:37,920
Mm.

461
00:41:39,000 --> 00:41:39,920
He won’t pick up my calls either.

462
00:41:46,840 --> 00:41:47,760
Why are you guys laughing?

463
00:41:48,840 --> 00:41:49,600
Nothing.

464
00:41:49,960 --> 00:41:52,720
It’s just... we’ve all been through this.

465
00:41:53,240 --> 00:41:55,960
Dean made us so irritated
and drove us crazy before.

466
00:41:58,280 --> 00:41:59,080
I’m not irritated.

467
00:42:01,160 --> 00:42:02,880
Okay. Whatever you say.

468
00:42:04,440 --> 00:42:05,760
Come on. Let’s drink.

469
00:42:06,200 --> 00:42:06,520
Come on.

470
00:42:07,320 --> 00:42:07,840
Cheers!

471
00:42:09,200 --> 00:42:10,960
Whoo!

472
00:42:16,480 --> 00:42:17,920
I’m not planning to get serious with Dean.

473
00:42:18,120 --> 00:42:18,760
I know.

474
00:42:19,720 --> 00:42:23,000
Who would get serious with Dean
unless they were an idiot?

475
00:42:33,080 --> 00:42:36,440
But at some point, you can’t help
but worry about him, right?

476
00:42:39,480 --> 00:42:41,240
No matter what you are to each other.

477
00:42:44,760 --> 00:42:45,800
That’s the turning point.

478
00:42:49,600 --> 00:42:50,080
Do you believe this?

479
00:42:51,480 --> 00:42:55,800
Some people are only
meant to cross our paths.

480
00:42:56,640 --> 00:42:57,840
They don’t deserve our concern.

481
00:42:59,240 --> 00:43:01,520
In the end,
Dean has to answer for his actions.

482
00:43:17,280 --> 00:43:17,760
All right.

483
00:43:18,880 --> 00:43:20,120
Let’s have the farewell drink.

484
00:43:21,640 --> 00:43:24,200
This round’s on the house.

485
00:43:24,480 --> 00:43:26,200
Since you guys are regulars.

486
00:43:27,000 --> 00:43:29,000
Wow!

487
00:43:29,840 --> 00:43:30,680
Farewell drink?

488
00:43:31,280 --> 00:43:32,080
Why?

489
00:43:32,600 --> 00:43:34,360
Tonight is our club’s last night.

490
00:43:34,880 --> 00:43:35,680
Our lease on this building is up.

491
00:43:37,960 --> 00:43:39,200
Come on. Whatever.

492
00:43:40,040 --> 00:43:45,120
(There are times when we feel like
we truly belong somewhere.)

493
00:43:46,880 --> 00:43:54,400
(But the truth is, when we’re gone,
that place doesn’t seem to miss us at all.)

494
00:44:01,560 --> 00:44:06,120
(There’s no place that belongs to us forever.)

495
00:44:09,280 --> 00:44:10,120
(No.)

496
00:44:12,520 --> 00:44:13,560
(I don’t think there is.)

497
00:44:26,320 --> 00:44:29,680
A WEEK LATER

498
00:44:34,760 --> 00:44:40,040
It can be anything,
as long as my activity is on your channel.

499
00:44:42,440 --> 00:44:44,080
Dean, I think…

500
00:44:49,160 --> 00:44:50,120
One hot cappuccino, please.

501
00:44:50,520 --> 00:44:51,800
We have a buy-one-get-one promotion.

502
00:44:51,800 --> 00:44:53,200
Would you like to get two?

503
00:44:53,800 --> 00:44:56,240
Oh, I’m here by myself.

504
00:44:58,080 --> 00:45:01,680
Can the other one be a caramel macchiato?

505
00:45:02,600 --> 00:45:03,920
Sure, of course.

506
00:45:03,920 --> 00:45:07,360
So, one hot cappuccino, and...

507
00:45:23,080 --> 00:45:23,720
- Hey!

508
00:45:23,800 --> 00:45:25,560
- You ditched work to
listen to Dr. Pun’s voice again.

509
00:45:25,560 --> 00:45:27,040
- You know he doesn’t like the real me.

510
00:45:27,400 --> 00:45:28,680
- It’s a blind date.

511
00:45:28,920 --> 00:45:29,480
- Interested?

512
00:45:29,600 --> 00:45:30,720
- I’ve got some free tickets.

513
00:45:30,720 --> 00:45:32,240
- Ask Pun to come.

514
00:45:32,360 --> 00:45:33,720
- Are you still playing cupid?

515
00:45:34,480 --> 00:45:35,200
- Go inside.

516
00:45:35,560 --> 00:45:36,040
- Hello.

517
00:45:36,720 --> 00:45:37,720
- Your voice sounds familiar.

518
00:45:38,080 --> 00:45:39,400
- Are you…?

519
00:45:39,400 --> 00:45:41,720
- Have you been avoiding me lately?

520
00:45:42,000 --> 00:45:43,120
- Why would I?

521
00:45:43,120 --> 00:45:45,080
